<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 5.150 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 5.150 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 5.150 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and nine repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    353 days   22.18 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    178 days</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     36 days</p>
<p>    500 million     35 days</p>
<p>    500 million     30 days</p>
<p>    550 million     28 days</p>
<p>    600 million     18 days</p>
<p>    600 million     16 days</p>
<p>    600 million     11 days</p>
<p>    700 million	4 days</p>
<p>    150 million	1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
